---
import DocumentSection from "../components/DocumentSection.astro";
import DocumentLayout from "../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro";
---

<DocumentLayout
  page="support"
  title="Support — Baros"
  description="Support information for Baros, a private workout tracker for iPhone."
  heading="Support"
  intro="Help for account access, sync, exports, local data, and account deletion in Baros."
>
  <DocumentSection title="Contact">
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:support@tatooles.dev">support@tatooles.dev</a> for
      support.
    </p>
    <p>
      We read every email. Include your device model, iOS version, what you were
      doing, and whether you were signed in when the issue happened.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Signing in and syncing">
    <ul>
      <li>You can log workouts locally without signing in.</li>
      <li>
        Signing in enables account-backed sync through the Baros production
        backend.
      </li>
      <li>
        If sync appears stuck, check your network connection, reopen the app, and
        confirm you are still signed in.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Exporting your data">
    <p>
      Workout history export is available from Settings. Export before deleting
      data if you want a personal copy of your workout history.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Local data and offline use">
    <p>
      Baros works without an account. If you stay signed out, workout history
      and settings remain local to your device unless you export or delete them
      from Settings.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Deleting your account">
    <p>
      Signed-in users can delete their account in the app from Settings under
      Privacy &amp; Data. Signed-out users can delete local data from the same
      area.
    </p>
    <p>
      Export first if you want to keep a personal copy of your workout history.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Privacy Policy">
    <p>
      Read the <a href="/privacy">Baros Privacy Policy</a> for details about
      local data, account data, sync, export, and deletion.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>
</DocumentLayout>
